1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,320
Your most expensive model just renamed

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:03,900
a variable.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,220
In the same chat, it judged

4
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:07,620
an authentication boundary.

5
00:00:07,993 --> 00:00:11,433
One chat, one model, every job.

6
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:13,593
That is why the bill is

7
00:00:13,593 --> 00:00:16,033
high, and the work gets worse.

8
00:00:16,509 --> 00:00:18,609
You didn't install a tool

9
00:00:19,229 --> 00:00:20,389
— you hired a manager.

10
00:00:21,249 --> 00:00:22,069
He runs the team;

11
00:00:22,729 --> 00:00:23,849
you only talk to him.

12
00:00:24,216 --> 00:00:26,416
He interviews you first

13
00:00:27,116 --> 00:00:29,156
— batches of at most four, each

14
00:00:29,156 --> 00:00:30,176
with his recommendation.

15
00:00:30,446 --> 00:00:32,166
Then he stops asking.

16
00:00:32,966 --> 00:00:35,046
The plan becomes tickets, on a

17
00:00:35,046 --> 00:00:35,431
board.

18
00:00:35,461 --> 00:00:37,421
Then the team goes out.

19
00:00:37,801 --> 00:00:39,121
A scout reads the repo.

20
00:00:39,901 --> 00:00:41,081
Cheap tier, read only.

21
00:00:41,330 --> 00:00:44,270
Implementers take one story each, on

22
00:00:44,270 --> 00:00:46,070
their own branch, with an empty

23
00:00:46,070 --> 00:00:46,690
scrollback.

24
00:00:47,390 --> 00:00:49,010
What they find goes into the

25
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:50,830
journal in your repo — so the

26
00:00:50,830 --> 00:00:53,410
reviewer starts already knowing it, and

27
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:55,510
a crash or a compaction changes

28
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:56,060
nothing.

29
00:00:56,216 --> 00:00:58,836
The reviewer grades the diff and

30
00:00:58,836 --> 00:00:59,916
cannot edit it.

31
00:01:00,316 --> 00:01:02,296
Otherwise it approves its own patch.

32
00:01:02,731 --> 00:01:04,691
A good manager doesn't put a

33
00:01:04,691 --> 00:01:06,331
principal engineer on a grep.

34
00:01:07,331 --> 00:01:09,251
Roles resolve to tiers, in one

35
00:01:09,251 --> 00:01:09,761
file.

36
00:01:09,791 --> 00:01:12,951
Security review always gets the strongest

37
00:01:12,951 --> 00:01:15,371
tier — and no flag or cost

38
00:01:15,371 --> 00:01:16,451
setting can lower it.

39
00:01:16,857 --> 00:01:18,917
All of it lands on one

40
00:01:18,917 --> 00:01:19,467
page.

41
00:01:20,257 --> 00:01:21,077
Five agents running.

42
00:01:21,757 --> 00:01:23,257
Two questions waiting on you.

43
00:01:23,549 --> 00:01:26,049
That card crossed into done by

44
00:01:26,049 --> 00:01:26,669
itself.

45
00:01:27,349 --> 00:01:28,569
Nobody dragged it there.

46
00:01:29,109 --> 00:01:29,769
This is Tyran,

47
00:01:30,409 --> 00:01:31,149
building Tyran.

48
00:01:31,491 --> 00:01:34,471
Halfway through, you remember something else.

49
00:01:34,731 --> 00:01:35,651
So you say it.

50
00:01:35,748 --> 00:01:38,168
It doesn't land in the scrollback.

51
00:01:38,728 --> 00:01:39,688
It becomes a ticket.

52
00:01:40,208 --> 00:01:41,428
Queued as T nine.

53
00:01:41,892 --> 00:01:44,052
A real decision comes back with

54
00:01:44,052 --> 00:01:44,692
a recommendation,

55
00:01:45,312 --> 00:01:45,862
not a shrug.

56
00:01:46,512 --> 00:01:48,172
You answer here, and the run

57
00:01:48,172 --> 00:01:48,772
carries on.

58
00:01:49,103 --> 00:01:50,563
Then the bill.

59
00:01:51,603 --> 00:01:53,283
Four and a half million tokens,

60
00:01:53,823 --> 00:01:56,183
across four hundred and four requests.

61
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,520
Fifty five percent of those tokens

62
00:01:58,520 --> 00:02:00,660
were the manager's own context.

63
00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:02,820
The manager gets its own row,

64
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,880
so nothing hides inside the total.

65
00:02:05,181 --> 00:02:08,521
The scout's whole reconnaissance cost three

66
00:02:08,521 --> 00:02:09,071
cents.

67
00:02:09,621 --> 00:02:10,601
This is not an estimate.

68
00:02:11,081 --> 00:02:12,021
It is the bill.

69
00:02:12,477 --> 00:02:15,417
Speak clearly at a natural pace

70
00:02:15,977 --> 00:02:18,157
with quiet confidence and a little

71
00:02:18,157 --> 00:02:18,707
warmth

72
00:02:19,877 --> 00:02:21,097
None of this is a prompt

73
00:02:21,097 --> 00:02:22,057
asking nicely.

74
00:02:22,737 --> 00:02:24,997
A hook decides before the tool

75
00:02:24,997 --> 00:02:25,777
ever runs.

76
00:02:25,956 --> 00:02:28,476
A commit carrying a secret is

77
00:02:28,476 --> 00:02:29,076
refused.

78
00:02:29,496 --> 00:02:31,036
Even inside a markdown file.

79
00:02:31,325 --> 00:02:33,765
A report with no command output

80
00:02:33,765 --> 00:02:35,065
is refused too.

81
00:02:35,705 --> 00:02:37,665
It blocks silence, not forgery.

82
00:02:38,070 --> 00:02:40,030
You try to close the session.

83
00:02:40,830 --> 00:02:41,380
It refuses.

84
00:02:42,410 --> 00:02:42,960
Once.

85
00:02:43,610 --> 00:02:45,810
The team runs the retrospective on

86
00:02:45,810 --> 00:02:46,360
itself.

87
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:48,260
One lesson is promoted.

88
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:50,220
One is rejected.

89
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:52,240
One is retired.

90
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:55,700
Work you keep asking for becomes

91
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:56,250
a skill.

92
00:02:56,532 --> 00:02:59,532
The same failure three times becomes

93
00:02:59,532 --> 00:03:00,082
knowledge.

94
00:03:00,932 --> 00:03:02,912
Five times, it becomes a rule

95
00:03:02,912 --> 00:03:03,572
in your repo.

96
00:03:04,038 --> 00:03:05,818
That was one request.

97
00:03:06,558 --> 00:03:07,978
You made two decisions.

98
00:03:08,618 --> 00:03:09,778
The team did the rest.

99
00:03:10,098 --> 00:03:12,578
Two commands inside Claude Code,

100
00:03:13,178 --> 00:03:14,798
then slash tyran setup.

101
00:03:15,378 --> 00:03:15,998
It's open source.
